    <!-- 09 Better for Brands -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="for-brands">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; For Brands</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Which is better for brands?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">It depends on what you are optimizing for. Here is a decision framework.</p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 mb-6">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4">
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-2 text-ink">Choose Traditional UGC if you:</h3>
            <ul class="pl-4 space-y-1.5 text-[13px] text-ink-2">
              <li>Need ad creative for an existing paid media funnel</li>
              <li>Have a small team and limited operational capacity</li>
              <li>Are in a regulated industry requiring legal review</li>
              <li>Want 5&ndash;20 high-quality videos per campaign</li>
              <li>Prioritize creative control over volume</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4">
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-2 text-ink">Choose Canvas UGC if you:</h3>
            <ul class="pl-4 space-y-1.5 text-[13px] text-ink-2">
              <li>Want to build an organic content engine</li>
              <li>Need 30&ndash;200+ videos per month</li>
              <li>Want to own the audience, not rent it</li>
              <li>Are willing to invest in a system that compounds</li>
              <li>Need the lowest possible cost per view at scale</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For brands serious about social media as a growth channel (not just a presence), canvas UGC is increasingly becoming the default. The model's compounding nature &mdash; owned audience, growing content library, improving algorithmic signal &mdash; makes it more valuable the longer you run it. Traditional UGC, by contrast, delivers value only for as long as you're paying for distribution.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">That said, nearly every brand can benefit from traditional UGC for targeted campaigns. The question is not which model to choose exclusively, but which one should be your primary organic strategy.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10 Better for Creators -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="for-creators">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">10 &mdash; For Creators</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Which is better for creators?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Both models offer legitimate income paths, but they reward different skills and work styles.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Factor</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Traditional UGC</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Canvas UGC</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Income ceiling</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Limited by hours (1 video = 1 payment)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Higher ceiling through volume + viral upside</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Income predictability</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Fixed rate per video &mdash; predictable</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Variable &mdash; depends on views</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Portfolio building</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Builds a <a href="/ugc-portfolio-guide/" class="text-accent hover:underline">portfolio</a> of brand work</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Builds proven performance metrics</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Skill development</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Scripting, filming, editing</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Hooks, trends, platform algorithms</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Getting started</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Need a portfolio and pitch to brands</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Apply to programs, start posting</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For creators who are strong content producers and understand what makes content go viral, canvas UGC offers a higher income ceiling. A creator posting across 3&ndash;5 brand accounts, producing 80&ndash;300 videos per month, can earn $3K&ndash;$15K+ monthly from aggregate views. The downside is variability &mdash; monthly income fluctuates with view counts.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For creators who prefer predictable income and enjoy the craft of producing polished content, traditional UGC offers more stability. You know exactly what each video pays before you film it. The tradeoff is a lower ceiling &mdash; each video requires time to produce, and income scales linearly with hours worked.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Many successful creators do both: traditional UGC for predictable baseline income, canvas UGC for upside potential. A <a href="/brand-pitch/" class="text-accent hover:underline">strong pitch</a> and <a href="/ugc-portfolio-guide/" class="text-accent hover:underline">portfolio</a> help with landing traditional UGC work, while canvas programs are more accessible to newer creators.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

